From 7ea775f8fb4b96bbf1cffa5acc1d956efa40dab9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LuneOS <claude.ai@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 23:34:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 17/17] com.webos.surfacemanager.groups.json: keep the array
 form our LS2 accepts

submissions/423 rewrote this file into a newer format where each group maps to
an object carrying trust/description/privacy. luna-service2 does not understand
that yet: the groups.schema it installs still requires each group to map to an
array of trust levels, so do_validate_ls2_security_conf rejects the file with
"isn't valid as per groups.schema" and the image fails to build.

This is not a LuneOS-only problem -- luna-service2 at submissions/47, the
version meta-webosose itself pins, ships the same array-form schema, so the
upstream pair is internally inconsistent.

Convert back to the array form, keeping the two groups 423 declares. The
surfacemanager.operation group 423 dropped is not restored: nothing in the tree
or the built rootfs requests any of these groups.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 base/sysbus/com.webos.surfacemanager.groups.json | 13 +++----------
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/base/sysbus/com.webos.surfacemanager.groups.json b/base/sysbus/com.webos.surfacemanager.groups.json
index 7864616..565187a 100644
--- a/base/sysbus/com.webos.surfacemanager.groups.json
+++ b/base/sysbus/com.webos.surfacemanager.groups.json
@@ -1,12 +1,5 @@
 {
-    "surfacemanager.devutility":{
-        "trust": "oem",
-        "description": "Provides development utilities for Surface manager",
-        "privacy": false
-    },
-    "surfacemanager.query":{
-        "trust": "oem",
-        "description": "Query status of Surface manager or a specific surface",
-        "privacy": false
-    }
+    "allowedNames": ["com.webos.surfacemanager*"],
+    "surfacemanager.devutility": ["oem"],
+    "surfacemanager.query": ["oem"]
 }
